Z||000003||Old Lar||09-21-2000||11:33 AM||||Lots of local transmission shops would be willing to rebuild/replace your automatic  get some quotes from the locals..expect $1000 for repair.  You may get a used one from Ed Parks, Bob Steiger or such..but those may need a rebuild anyway from a 12-16 year old doner car.||||reg||4
Z||000004||theogre||09-21-2000||07:23 PM||||You can put any TH125 in it. You just need to change the shift arm and brackets. (The TV cable to depending on what motor the tranny was on.) You might even want to look into other threads in here about putting one of the 4 speed autos in.<P>The only thing you want to find out if you can is what final drive is in the tranny. That's in the option codes of the car it's in. You may also be able to run numbers off the tranny's tag and get the info. (It's not a huge issue what gears they are in most cases. There are only 3 choices.<P>All TH125 transmissions are essentially the same except for the final drive gears. The following RPO codes apply to TH125c and 440 T4 transmission final drive gears.<P>FP3, FW2, FW9, F47, F90 = 3.06 <P>F16, F17, F62, F75 = 2.84<P>F77, F79, GX3 = 3.33<P>||||reg||1
